// `member: target` bridges a *user* trait's required method onto a member; a built-in has no
// member to bridge, so the binding is E0050 at the binding itself. The two built-in shapes differ
// in what the help then offers — `Comparable` delegates through a field, `Validate` does not, and
// suggesting `via:` for `Validate` would only send the reader to a second error.
// expect: error E0050 at 8:21
// expect: error E0050 at 11:19
// expect: exit 1
@derive(Comparable, compare: v)
struct Reading { v: int }

@derive(Validate, validate: v)
struct Tally { v: int }

echo "unreached"
